  "external_reference_note": "The C++ driver, its build, the disassembly, the libstdc++ headers the port transcribes and the raw outputs live outside this repository under ../oracle/sne-completion/; only the case files, the vector file and the two result files enter the repository, byte for byte. The build ran on ibminode06 (never ibminode05) against the unmodified Release install below. previous-run-1/ there holds the first capture of 123 cases, which the second capture reproduces byte for byte for every one of those cases.",
  "oracle": {
    "release_install": "/ceph/ibmi/abi/oliver/opt/openms4-release-bc9cc12-c19e494-174b576",
    "pins": {
      "core": "bc9cc12",
      "cli": "c19e494",
      "topp": "174b576"
    },
    "libOpenMS_so_sha256": "abd4fc9977823c793b4396586210a867cf72482cd3ab228d6aec8ddb54966d6c",
    "host": "ibminode06, Linux 6.8.0-124-generic x86_64",
    "compiler": "x86_64-conda-linux-gnu-g++ (conda-forge gcc 14.4.0-4) 14.4.0, the toolchain of the Release build",
    "compile_options": "-O3 -DNDEBUG -std=gnu++23 -fPIC -fvisibility=hidden -fvisibility-inlines-hidden -mssse3 -ffp-contract=off -fopenmp, the flags of SignalToNoiseEstimator.cpp in the Release build's build/core/compile_commands.json, so that the header-only estimator the driver instantiates is compiled as libOpenMS compiles its own copies",
    "driver_sha256": "7866d64cbed28cf2ae3877a6f340faf8a037848f121f770f290939974a47907f",
    "driver_binary_sha256": "571d6f9be37534cfc99d1f0e3ffc9e37179788865b5f3f925bc982a53038278c",
    "time_interposition": "the driver exports time() (-rdynamic, default visibility); libOpenMS resolves its time@plt to it, so the seed of estimateNoiseFromRandomScans and the ProgressLogger throttle read the value each case sets",
    "runs": 2,
    "fresh_process_per_case": true,
    "reproduced_byte_for_byte": true,
    "cases": 143,
    "nth_vectors": 390,
    "comparison": "every ratio, max_intensity_, percentage, random-scan result, engine output, uniform draw, picked peak and boundary as an IEEE-754 bit pattern; the whole nth_element permutation; standard error byte for byte against the port's warnings rendered through LogStream; standard output byte for byte against the port's ProgressLogger with the two timings masked",
    "p1_rerun": "the unchanged P1 driver (sha256 2d06db2f...) against the same Release install, twice: records byte-identical to the arm64 Debug capture (sha256 9eb8f249...), the same two parameter files, and a standard error that differs only by six mzML loader lines the Debug build alone prints",
    "probes": "thirteen out-of-domain inputs, three runs each, exit codes and record digests only (probes/results.txt); not fixtures"
  },
  "determinism": "The estimator and the random-scan estimate are serial, as the source is (no OpenMP in either header or in SignalToNoiseEstimator.cpp); the random-scan estimate takes its seed as an argument."
}
